"Before Badud's deal, the Ending of History was due at Gemore about a thousand years off."
"Later, Badud's deal brings the Ending of History forward to strike Gemore within a century."
"Later, Nathan teaches Gemore's crafters to make firearms, and guns become common there."
"Later, Brox is given stewardship of Gemore; years later the Heirs displace him."
"Later, the Heirs found a library of Insights in Gemore and copy their physics book there."
"Later, Gemore and the empire of Agmon go to war."
"Years later, a council of the masters of Gemore's seven guilds rules it from a curved stone table."
"Years later, the Guardians of Gemore defend the city."
"Years later, Gemore forbids selling items of vast destructive power."
"Years later, Gemore's law requires people not to inflict their costs on others."
"Years later, the Adventurer's Guild building has become the Archive, a hall of engineering classes."
"Years later, Gemore's steelmill runs on fire enchantments, air magic, bessemer and charcoal."
"Years later, Gemore arc-forges with electricity mana and alloys Edrani construct wreckage."
"Years later, Poppy's chemical works in Gemore make cordite in bulk to crack dungeons."
"Years later, fifteen-foot steam-powered armored suits in Gemore level their wearers very fast."
"Years later, a few dozen metal-mana mages can raise a Gemore building in days."
"Years later, lightning spikes top Gemore's new wall towers, and air magic lifts its smoke away."
"Years later, villagers near Gemore carry guns of new design, and Gemore folk shout \"Hail the Heirs!\""
